Included upstream modules:
- packages/relay: original source, tests, fixtures and configuration.
- packages/app/src/components/markdown/image-decoding.ts.
- packages/client: complete original package source, including its tests.
- packages/protocol: complete original package source, including its tests,
  fixtures and generator scripts.
- packages/server: secure-relay-ingress, encrypted-relay-socket,
  physical-socket, relay-transport, daemon-keypair, private-files,
  connection-offer and network dependency closure, with corresponding tests.

Workbench adaptations:
- Relay package.json is private, removes prepack and pins runtime dependency
  versions. Original manifest is retained as package.upstream.json.
- Relay source is unchanged. Dist JavaScript and declarations were generated
  with TypeScript 5.9.3. Workbench host/client wrappers request protected mode;
  they do not replace device enrollment or command authorization.
- The unchanged image decoder receives Workbench's authenticated Blob URL and
  DOM Image.decode adapter in apps/web/src/components/Attachments.tsx.
- Client and protocol original runtime sources are unchanged. Their manifests
  are private, reference local Paseo dependencies, pin installed runtime
  versions and remove automatic lifecycle hooks. Original manifests remain
  as package.upstream.json. Client internal exports expose the transport family.
- The server transport package has a private dependency-closure manifest with
  no lifecycle scripts. relay-transport.ts changes one type-only import to an
  exact extraction of ExternalSocketMetadata. Its runtime statements are
  unchanged, and its byte-exact original is retained under upstream/.
- A separate client compatibility helper extracts the original reconnect
  defaults and delay calculation. The full original DaemonClient connection
  state machine and SDK application-protocol facade remain unconnected.
- Added tsconfig.workbench.json files select the required transport/protocol
  entry points and their dependency closure. Existing standalone JavaScript
  and declaration outputs are recorded with file SHA-256 hashes. Original
  upstream tsconfig files remain unchanged. The selected compile does not
  execute the retained upstream lifecycle or validator-generation scripts.
- Workbench adapters use the original protected WebSocket/E2EE and outgoing
  relay implementations. The original server_info schema precedes Workbench's
  separate device authorization, request/reply and event-subscription protocol.

Source and generated file hashes are in relay-provenance.json,
image-decoding-provenance.json, client-provenance.json,
protocol-provenance.json and server-provenance.json. The latter three also
record the added compile configurations and selected compilation scope.

Installed runtime dependency licenses and notices are preserved under
dependencies/; actual package versions and copied-file SHA-256 hashes are in
dependencies.json. This includes pino and its installed helper dependencies,
zod, semver, undici (including its embedded fetch license), https-proxy-agent
and its dependency closure, and qrcode 1.5.4 with its installed dependencies.
Distinct installed versions have separate entries. Optional ws peers
bufferutil and utf-8-validate were not installed in this attribution snapshot.

These are Workbench attribution and modification notices. Original copyright
notices and licenses are preserved in the imported sources and copied licenses.

Terminal module bundle added at the same pinned revision:
- Original app TerminalStreamController, TerminalEmulatorRuntime, keyboard,
  virtual keyboard, local-link and file-paste dependency closure.
- Original server headless terminal, serializer, resize ownership and
  local-service connector. DA/DSR/color handlers are directly extracted from
  terminal.ts and receive the existing owned-worker input port.
- Original source is byte-preserved under vendor/paseo/terminal/upstream.
  Compatibility src uses ESM paths and narrow type ports; embedded-pane style,
  existing selection/scroll access, existing regex/case options and replay
  commit callback are explicit adaptations. A declaration shim resolves
  the original ligatures mjs import without replacing runtime behavior.
- Workbench retains its existing worker supervisor, workspace ownership,
  bounded SQLite byte journal and device grants. The public Paseo hostname
  proxy listener and PTY supervisor are not started.
- Exact resolved xterm/addon dependencies and generated module hashes are in
  terminal-provenance.json. Dependency MIT/ISC/Apache notices are copied under
  dependencies with versioned paths. Local-link modules retain Microsoft MIT
  notices. Headless/serialize published packages contain no separate license
  file; their shared xterm MIT notice is preserved from the xterm package.
- The new loopback fixture is not native/device acceptance. Full browser
  preview and WebSocket/HMR service tunnelling are not supplied by this port.

Workbench 0.4.0 mobile and service integration:
- Original mobile IME, file classification, viewport and download helper functions: mobile-web/source.json and NOTICE.
- Original push token lease/store and delivery injection: push/source.json; Workbench supplies standard web-push transport.
- Original outbound Hub relationship, reconnect and execution controller: hub/source.json.

Paseo Hub relationship reuse (U24)
Original enrollment/authenticated WebSocket/heartbeat/retry/revocation and execution
controllers, authorization table and provider-option helpers are reused under
vendor/paseo/server. Type-only ports and a required Workbench OS-vault record codec
are the adapter boundary. Source and adaptation hashes are in hub/source.json;
original source bytes remain under vendor/paseo/server/upstream/hub-reuse.
